{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":15067130,"ns":0,"title":"Antoine's necklace","extract":"In mathematics, Antoine's necklace is a topological embedding of the Cantor set in 3-dimensional Euclidean space, whose complement is not simply connected. It also serves as a counterexample to the claim that all Cantor spaces are ambiently homeomorphic to each other.","description":"Embedding of Cantor set in 3-dimensional Euclidean space","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}